    {
      "id": "BPP-02",
      "chapter": "normalization",
      "anchor": "normalization-branching-period-translate",
      "title": "A bounded translate has a quantitatively large branching projection",
      "hypotheses": "The mixed moment of BPP-01, formal-degree orthogonality on both unitary groups, the subgroup formal-degree comparison, the ambient Haar ball bound and the signed-unitary stabilizer geometry for the distinguished positive unit vector.",
      "statement": "There exists g₀ with ‖g₀‖F≤X^(10m) and ‖i*π(g₀)v₀‖≥X^(−100m³). In particular ℬ(100)‖i*π(g₀)v₀‖≥1 for ℬ(100)=X^(100m⁴).",
      "definitions": [
        "Choose Y₁=2X^(8m), D=X^(67m²), K=4X^(24m³). At least half the Schur mass lies where ‖g⁻¹z‖²≤Y₁.",
        "The finite-volume region C is defined by ‖g‖F²≤64m(m+Y₁)² and U by ‖h−1‖F≤1. Translating its indicator yields ν(U)∫S F ≤ ∫C∫H F(ι(h)k)."
      ],
