  "outstanding": [
    "SBO-01 through SBO-03 explain propagation of signed occurrence and recovery of an intertwiner from a nonzero integral. The distant initial occurrence, the smaller-group lowering and the smooth seed identity remain upstream. STM-01 through STM-03 track the signed tensor decomposition, ratios of formal degrees and the resulting component mass. BVD-01 through BVD-03 give the two derivative budgets. The quantum cofactor and its specialization explain the entrywise projection bound used in STM-03.",
    "BPP-02 uses two separate ball estimates for distinct Haar measures and degrees. The proof derives the quantitative translation from these and the mixed moment. The named constants are valid in the indicated model and parameter range.",
    "The finite-dimensional circle example isolates the eigenvector normalization and does not instantiate the large-gap unitary branching hypotheses."
  ]
}
